                <pb facs="0874" n="788" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg788"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr.
                            Bowen.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-12-01"><hi rendition="#italic">December 1,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hill instructs Mr. Bowen, in case of diplomatic rupture between Germany and
                    Venezuela, to exercise the same good offices for Germany as for Great Britain,
                    with the consent of the Venezuelan Government.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
